# Project Architecture

## Tech stack

- Static site hosted on GitHub Pages at `shuffleo.github.io/leolau.hk` (no build step); `leolau.hk` redirects to it but does not serve content directly
- Client-side Markdown rendering via Marked.js (loaded from jsDelivr CDN)
- Extended table support via `marked-extended-tables`
- Shared `app.js` and `styles.css` at repo root, referenced by all pages

## Site structure

- `/` — homepage (`index.html` + `content.md`)
- `/writings/` — listing page + individual essay subpages
- `/works/` — listing page (custom table with hover previews) + individual work subpages

## URL system (Notion-style)

- Folders: `{title-slug}-{32-char-hex-id}/` — created once, never renamed
- Generate IDs with `openssl rand -hex 16`
- Browser URL auto-updates to current title via `history.replaceState` (`updateUrlSlug()` in `app.js`)
- Stale-slug URLs resolve via `404.html` → `articles.json` lookup → redirect

### Cosmetic URL vs. on-disk folder (do not regress)

The address bar path can become **longer than the real folder name** (full title slug + id), while GitHub Pages only serves files under the **original** directory. After `replaceState`, the document URL no longer matches that directory.

- **Markdown images** use relative `src` (e.g. `![alt](./photo.webp)`). The browser resolves them against the **current** URL, so they would 404 under the cosmetic path unless fixed.
- **Mitigation:** `app.js` snapshots the deployed entry path at load (`__LEO_ENTRY_ASSET_BASE`) and rewrites relative `<img src>` in `improveImageHandling()` before requests fire. Do **not** remove this without an equivalent fix (e.g. absolute asset URLs generated at build time).
- **`fetch('content.md')`** runs before `replaceState`, so body text still loads; the pitfall is mainly **relative assets** after the URL changes.
- **Verify** entry pages on the real Pages base path (`shuffleo.github.io/leolau.hk/.../`) when changing URL or image pipeline code, especially works with long `#` titles vs. short folder slugs.

## Adding content

- New article: create folder, add `content.md` (with `# Title` and `Published: YYYY-MM-DD`), run `python3 update-subpages.py`
- Title change: edit `# Title` in `content.md`, run `python3 update-subpages.py` — no folder rename needed
- Works entries: also add a `preview.webp` and manually update `works/content.md` table

## Image loading

- All `.webp` images get blur-up loading: a `*-tiny.webp` placeholder (~32px) shows instantly, full image fades in on load
- Naming convention: `photo.webp` → `photo-tiny.webp`, `preview.webp` → `preview-tiny.webp`
- `optimize-images.py --run` generates missing tiny thumbnails automatically
- Works hover previews also use blur-up (two-layer: `preview-tiny.webp` + `preview.webp`)

## SEO meta tags

- `update-subpages.py` generates `<meta>` description, Open Graph (`og:title`, `og:description`, `og:url`, `og:image`), and Twitter Card tags in every `index.html`
- Description: first body paragraph after the `---` separator, stripped of markdown formatting, truncated to 155 chars
- Image: first `.webp` image in the markdown, or `preview.webp` as fallback — used as `og:image` with absolute URL
- Root `index.html` has hand-written OG tags

## YouTube embed behavior

- Bare YouTube URLs in markdown → embedded player (iframe)
- YouTube URLs with custom anchor text like `[text](youtube-url)` → plain hyperlink
